+ * lowest troop stack's HP: *"2 % seems fair but could be configurable without clogging the ui, maybe hidden for now
+ * and conduct an experiment"*).
+ *
+ * `CAMPAIGN.shelterMargin` (`src/config.ts`, `CampaignInput.shelterMargin`): every hired stack stands strictly under
+ * `floor × (1 − margin)`. Every benchmark army is planned as the app plans it (`CAMPAIGN.planFixes`, the put-back at
+ * the app's rates), `budgetMs` off, at margins 0, 1 %, 2 % and 5 %. Against margin 0: every stop by `rate()`, the ten
+ * readings, TotalStack at matched spend, the bar's criteria (169's), the owner's tier-twin test (`tier-twin.ts`),
+ * and the margins the bar actually stands at. The owner's two camps in full. At margin 0 the bar is also compared,
+ * byte for byte, with HEAD's (3c4b23d, from a worktree), to hold that the setting moves nothing when it is 0.
+ *
+ * Two phases, so the four margins run in four processes:
+ *
+ * `M173=0.02 THEORY=1 npx vitest run tools/theorycraft/173-a-shelter-margin.test.ts` — plans one margin, dumps it;
+ * `R173=1 THEORY=1 npx vitest run tools/theorycraft/173-a-shelter-margin.test.ts` — reads the four dumps, writes
+ * `out/173-a-shelter-margin.md`. `WT173` is the HEAD worktree (node_modules linked), `D173` the dump folder.
+ */
